title: A test of skg on a stranger takes weeks, not an hour, and fails on what the stranger would give up, not on the interface.
pid: 98330750-1f07-4ae9-8a68-828ea375dfae
body: |2-
  His sixth cause, with his example: ten members of a lab
  usability-tested a co-authoring tool that then went unused, because
  some had the wrong computer and the rest would not give up their
  word processor; "They were fine-tuning the interface to an
  application that would not be used." For skg the question is what a
  stranger keeps notes in now ('docs/who-maps-knowledge.org' lists
  Obsidian, Notion, org-roam and others) and whether they would move;
  'docs/setup.org' imports from org-roam. The test is an action in
  Ed's action subgraph, "Watch one person who is not Jeff use skg,
  unrequired, for some weeks."
